Planning reconciliation — 2026-08-12 America/Sao_Paulo

User authorized this planning-only batch and set a conditional product requirement: any future Eon-owned editor engine must retain Helix-like modal editing and most Helix default keybindings whether or not it reuses helix-core.

Applied without activating implementation:
- expanded eon-ofb with the durable semantic editor contract, ownership map, exact Helix evidence, primary architecture comparisons, candidate shapes, negative scope, and first falsifiable proof;
- created eon-specify-helix-modal-semantics-3kl;
- created eon-preserve-helix-keybindings-uca;
- ordered modal semantics -> keybinding continuity -> eon-ofb;
- kept all three deferred at P3, with Helix remaining the accepted EON-C4 editor.

Reconciliation: eon-pxn already owns Eon workspace and AgentRun composition, eon-az9 owns isolated execution targets, and eon-decide-eon-session-durability-qhf owns supervisor/reboot/machine-loss durability. No duplicate agent, workspace, isolation, durability, Venus implementation, repository, dependency, or product-contract Bead was created.

Second fresh-eyes convergence — 2026-08-26 UTC

Formatting correction: the implementation and first fresh-eyes comments at 00:05 and 00:17 UTC contain literal `\n` text because their multiline messages were passed through the CLI incorrectly. `br` has no comment edit or delete operation. This correctly formatted note supersedes their presentation; the later comment already corrects the invalid manifest command recorded by the earlier one.

Confirmed omissions fixed in the existing single EONW v3 test:

- round-trip the ordinary snapshot state with no directory picker;
- round-trip the v3 failure response that uses the shared failure codec;
- reject an empty picker endpoint;
- reject an endpoint one byte above the 4096-byte bound;
- retain the existing present-picker, wrong-tab, pane-alias, cross-version, lifecycle, all-action, and maximum-frame checks.

Simplification: v3 now imports its private v2 codec owner once at module scope and includes `declared_message_len` in the existing public re-export list, removing eight repeated import/export lines. Wrapping v2 actions, adding a common module, removing captured-tab identity, or splitting the one contract test still fails the complexity or proof gate.

Verification on Eon HEAD `df72e525eb510b2e57e3b2bb33a309140e083052` dirty candidate:

- focused EONW test and clippy pass;
- full fmt, locked workspace check/test/clippy, and the correct manifest-path validator pass;
- `nix flake check --print-build-logs` passes against the final staged v3 source, including exact Venus `19d7d28a2aba09c0afe3173d25bbb76ec3edce49` and 110 tests, Eon/EonTerm packages and tests, managed-command-path, shell environment, and closure checks;
- `git diff --check` and LOC recount pass: Rust 9,786; repository total 13,211.

The production codec is smaller; the missing boundary cases account for the retained total LOC. A final clean reread found no remaining confirmed defect or simplification with a positive proof/risk tradeoff. No installed runtime or profile changed. The feature remains deferred pending immutable seed publication and the separate exact Venus consumer.
